{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "20", "m": "10", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "13", "M": "06", "S": "19"}}, "news": [{"title": "Over 2,500 flats booked under Delhi development body's Awas Nivesh housing scheme", "para": "On October 20, the Delhi Development Authority unveiled the Awas Nivesh Yojana 2026 to promote affordable housing initiatives. Within just two hours of its launch, over 2,500 flats targeted at the Low Income Group were booked online, thanks to a lucrative 25 percent discount. This scheme showcases a strong commitment to making quality housing attainable for families in need, reflecting the persistent demand for affordable options in Delhi.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/over-2500-flats-booked-under-delhi-development-bodys-awas-nivesh-housing-scheme/135070543?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-226072/135070543.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Only 53 of over 2,400 PGs submitted structural safety certificates: Delhi civic body", "para": "In response to a recent collapse in Satya Niketan, the MCD conducted a survey of 2,457 PG accommodations to assess structural safety. Only 53 provided the necessary safety certificates before the deadline. This initiative aims to reduce risks and ensure adherence to building codes. With limited staff for audits, MCD plans to take action against violators next month and is developing stricter policies for older buildings.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/only-53-of-over-2400-pgs-submitted-structural-safety-certificates-delhi-civic-body/135061393?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-205534/135061393.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "NCDRC orders fresh completion certificates for Purab Premium Apartments", "para": "The National Consumer Disputes Redressal Commission has mandated Gmada to re-evaluate the completion certificates for Purab Premium Apartments. This ruling comes after addressing issues related to compensation and maintenance charges for residents. Gmada is required to confirm that all promised amenities are in place before issuing new certificates. Concerns have been raised by residents regarding the certificates issued back in October 2024.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/regulatory/ncdrc-orders-fresh-completion-certificates-for-purab-premium-apartments/135061364?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-101579/135061364.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "regulatory"}]}